  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Wealthy oligarch Danila Alyokhin arrives at the hotel lobby with a remarkably heavy wedding gift box for Eleonora and Nagiyev: a red brick containing a solid gold bar to fund their St. Petersburg hotel project.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Дима, олигарх приехал!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Как я рада вас видеть!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Мое поздравление молодоженам.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Одно ваше присутствие — это уже подарок.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Ух ты, тяжелый подарок.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Там золотой слиток?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Можете взглянуть.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Это просто кирпич.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Это непростой кирпич, а внутри золотой слиток.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "И я готов его финансировать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Боже мой, спасибо вам огромное!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Я приехал с супругой, а вот она.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Дима, олигарх приехал!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Dima, the oligarch has arrived!' Eleonora anchors the line on 'Dima', while 'came' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Как я рада вас видеть!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'How glad I am to see you!' The grammar packs 'how' and 'to see' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Мое поздравление молодоженам.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'My congratulations to the newlyweds.' The meaning hinges on 'my' working together with 'newlyweds' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Одно ваше присутствие — это уже подарок.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Your presence alone is already a gift.' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'one' and finishing on 'gift'. Dmitry Nagiyev answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Ух ты, тяжелый подарок.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Wow, it is a heavy gift.' Dmitry Nagiyev anchors the line on 'oh', while 'gift' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Там золотой слиток?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Is there a gold ingot in there?' The grammar packs 'there' and 'ingot' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Можете взглянуть.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You may take a look.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'can' before landing on 'to take a look'. Dmitry Nagiyev answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Это просто кирпич.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'It is just a brick.' Dmitry Nagiyev brings out the contrast between 'this' and 'simply' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Это непростой кирпич, а внутри золотой слиток.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'It is no ordinary brick, and inside is a gold ingot.' the guest anchors the line on 'this', while 'ingot' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "И я готов его финансировать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And I am ready to finance it.' The grammar packs 'and' and 'to finance' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange. Eleonora answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Боже мой, спасибо вам огромное!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Oh my goodness, thank you so much!' Eleonora brings out the contrast between 'God' and 'my' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Я приехал с супругой, а вот она.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I arrived with my wife, and here she is.' In Russian, the idea of 'I' flows naturally into 'she' without extra filler words. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
